  "chunk": "based gameplay, with LLM-models showing behaviour that differs substantially\nfrom expected human behaviour. However, the extent to which these domain-\nspecific limitations reflect broader constraints remains an open question.\n6 Limitations\nThis positioning paper has several limitations that should be acknowledged. Our\nexperimental design includes five runs per setting, which limits statistical power\nand prevents definitive claims about the absence of differences between settings.\nMoreover, we lack human player baselines, making it difficult to contextualize\nwhether an average∼10% completion represents failure or reasonable perfor-\nmance on a genuinely difficult game. We cannot rule out training data contam-\nination, as models may have encountered Zork walkthroughs during training,\nalthough the established performance suggests little to no contamination. Our\nqualitative analysis draws on illustrative examples rather than systematic analy-",
